  "summary": "The regulatory and competitive landscape continues shifting rapidly across healthcare. The FTC is cracking down on price transparency with warning letters to 24 healthcare organizations, while Congress advanced the Health Care Cybersecurity and Resilience Act as hospitals face increasingly sophisticated AI-driven cyber threats that outpace traditional disaster recovery planning. Meanwhile, significant consolidation is reshaping specific sectors: PBM market concentration has intensified with four companies now controlling 75 percent of the market, and major pharma continues aggressive M&A activity with Shionogi's $2 billion acquisition in rare diseases and Sanofi's $1 billion expansion of its Regeneron alliance. On the innovation front, venture capital continues to fund emerging health-tech companies despite broader VC headwinds, with notable rounds going to AI-focused firms like WhiteLab Genomics and Parakeet Health, alongside traditional healthcare tech addressing interoperability, microbiome testing, and food-as-medicine programs. The FDA is preparing new AI guidance for 2027 and recruiting fresh voices for advisory committees, reflecting broader efforts to update regulatory frameworks for an increasingly technology-driven healthcare system.",
